  <text xml:lang="ta" type="edition">
    <body>

        <div xml:id="AN224.1-kilavi">
          <p type="edition">viṉaimuṟṟiya talaimakaṉ ṟērpākaṟkuc colliyatu.</p>
          <p type="translation" xml:lang="en">What HE who had completed work said to [his] charioteer.</p>
        </div>
        <div rend="parallel">
      <lg xml:id="AN224.1">
        <l>celka pāka velliṉṟu poḻutē</l>
        <l>vallō ṉaṭaṅkukayi ṟamaippak kollaṉ</l>
        <l>micaittuvāṅku turuttiyiṉ veyya vuyirāk</l>
        <l>koṭunukat tiyātta talaiya kaṭunaṭaik</l>
        <l>kā[ṟ]kaṭup paṉṉa kaṭuñcela livuḷi</l>
        <l>pālkaṭai nuraiyiṉ parūu[mi]tap paṉṉa</l>
        <l>vālveṇ ṭeviṭṭal vaḻivāratu nuṇakkañ</l>
        <l>cilampi [nū]li ṉuṇaṅkuvaṉa pāṟic</l>
        <l>cāntupula rakala maṟuppak kāṇṭakap</l>
        <l>putunalam peṟṟa peytunīṅku puṟaviṟ</l>
        <l>ṟeṟinaṭa maraikkaṇa miriya maṉaiyō</l>
        <l>ḷaituṇaṅku valci peytumuṟuk kuṟutta</l>
        <l>tirimarak kuralicai kaṭuppa varimaṇa</l>
        <l>lalaṅkukatirt tikiri yāḻi pōḻa</l>
        <l>varuṅko ṟōḻinam miṉṉuyirt tuṇaiyeṉac</l>
        <l>cilkō lelvaḷai yoṭukkip palkā</l>
        <l>laruṅkaṭi viyaṉa[ka]r nōkki</l>
        <l>varuntumā laḷiya ṭiruntiḻai tāṉē.</l>
      </lg>
      <lg type="translation" xml:lang="en">
        <l corresp="1">Let [us] go, charioteer – It is the time without light! –</l>
        <l corresp="10">through the woodland that had obtained fresh beauty, abandoned [by the clouds] after raining</l>
        <l corresp="9d">fit to be seen, while</l>
        <l corresp="5">by the horses with a movement swift as the speed of wind,</l>
        <l corresp="4">with swift gait, [their] heads tied to the curved yoke,</l>
        <l corresp="2d-3">breathing as hot as the bellows pulled on top by the smith</l>
        <l corresp="2a-c">while the capable [driver] handles the restraining rope,</l>
        <l rend="indent2" corresp="8">[droplets] are scattered fine like the thread of a spider,</l>
        <l corresp="7">something long [and] fine [resulting] from pure white spitter</l>
        <l corresp="6">like big floats of foam on the rim of milk,</l>
        <l corresp="9ac">[and] stain the chest on which sandal dries,</l>
        <l corresp="14">so that the round [chariot] wheels with flashing spokes cross</l>
        <l corresp="13">the lined sand, resembling in tone the voice of the mill</l>
        <l>set into whirling [motion] as she of the house pours wonderfully</l>
        <l corresp="11f">dry grains, so that the groups of wild cows that walk in leaps retreat.</l>
        <l corresp="18">She will be suffering indeed, pitiful she, she with perfect jewels,</l>
        <l corresp="17">looking [out] from the well-protected wide mansion,</l>
        <l corresp="16">many times, checking [her] bright bangles in a few rows,</l>
        <l corresp="15">saying “is he coming, friend, our companion [as] dear as life?”</l>
      </lg>
        </div>
